dts: cut the display CMA pool from 6 MB to 4 MB

Copy esp32s31.dtsi back over
linux-71-port/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dtsi before building.
A DTS change needs BOTH `make linux` AND `make opensbi` - the kernel uses a
builtin DTB, so rebuilding only OpenSBI leaves the old tree in force.

WHY
Memory is the binding constraint on this board: 15,412 kB total, of which
4,244 is unreclaimable slab. The display pool was 6 MB with 3,128 kB of it
free at idle, and CmaFree does not count as headroom (see
s31-watermark-boost-oom).

WHY THE OLD FAILURE DOES NOT APPLY
The node recorded a specific failure at 4 MB: three contiguous 768 kB
allocations in flight at 800x480 - the driver's scanout buffer, fbdev
emulation's console framebuffer, and THE DESKTOP'S OWN render target - with
the third failing as "CREATE_DUMB: Out of memory". That third allocation was
Xorg's. lvdesk presents through the driver's own fullscreen buffer and never
makes it.

Verified on kernel #198: boots, takes DRM master, runs a fullscreen client
through a full timedemo with no CREATE_DUMB failure, no "scaling off", no CMA
allocation failure. CmaFree 1,096 kB of 4,096 under load, so the working set
is ~2.8 MB - the same as the 6 MB pool showed.

STILL OWED
A settled fresh-boot-per-arm measurement of available memory. The two idle
samples taken so far had very different page-cache histories and non-CMA free
came out slightly LOWER at 4 MB, which is the wrong direction and is probably
the comparison rather than the change.
